{% comment %}
  The mark — Section Two. Gold seed, two purple rings, one gold outer ring,
  gap at the top. Ring radii step 1.6x outward from the seed; every arc runs
  20deg to 340deg so the opening is centred and identical on all three.

  These three path values are NOT computed here. Liquid has no sin/cos, so
  the arc geometry is precomputed once in Python (the same arc() function
  that generates the GitHub Pages site) and hardcoded below. Verified
  byte-for-byte identical to that function's output before being pasted in
  — see the theme README for the verification command. Do not hand-edit
  these coordinates; regenerate them from arc() if the geometry ever changes.

  Colour is NOT a parameter here, on purpose — it matches assets/theme.css,
  ported unchanged from the GitHub Pages site: .on-purple .mark and
  .on-gold .mark are ANCESTOR selectors. The mark reads its colour from
  whatever section wraps it (a section with class on-purple or on-gold), the
  same way it works on the current live site. Wrap the call, don't pass a
  variant — there isn't one to pass.

  Usage:
    {% render 'mark', size: 104, draw: true %}          hero, draws once on load
    {% render 'mark', size: 32, rings_lock: 3 %}         header, reduction overridden
    {% render 'mark', size: 44, rings_lock: 2 %}         footer
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign m_size = size | default: 104
-%}
<svg
  class="mark{% if extra_class %} {{ extra_class }}{% endif %}"
  viewBox="0 0 100 100"
  width="{{ m_size }}"
  height="{{ m_size }}"
  role="img"
  aria-label="monk manthra"
  {% if draw %}data-draw=""{% endif %}
  {% if rings_lock %}data-rings="{{ rings_lock }}" data-rings-lock=""{% endif %}
  focusable="false"
>
  <path class="ring ring--1" d="M 54.788 36.844 A 14.0 14.0 0 1 1 45.212 36.844"/>
  <path class="ring ring--2" d="M 57.661 28.951 A 22.4 22.4 0 1 1 42.339 28.951"/>
  <path class="ring ring--3" d="M 62.258 16.321 A 35.84 35.84 0 1 1 37.742 16.321"/>
  <circle class="seed" cx="50" cy="50" r="5.2"/>
</svg>
